          <p>
            Here are a few excersises for Back
            <!-- video embed for excersises in back -->
            • Latissimus Dorsi (Lats):
            Location: Large muscles on the sides and mid-back that create the classic V-shape or upper-body taper.
            Best Exercises: Lat pulldowns, pull-ups (or assisted pull-ups), and dumbbell pullovers.

            • Trapezius (Traps):
            Location: Spans the back of the neck, shoulders, and mid-back.
            Best Exercises: Face pulls, resistance band pull-aparts, and upright rows.

            • Rhomboids:
            Location: Located right between your shoulder blades.
            Best Exercises: Seated cable rows, single-arm dumbbell rows, and bent-over rows.

            • Erector Spinae (Lower Back):
            Location: Runs vertically down both sides of your spine.
            Best Exercises: Conventional deadlifts, Romanian deadlifts, bodyweight Supermans, and back extensions.
          </p>
