            <!-- video embed for lowerbody -->
            Quadriceps (Front of Thighs)

            • Anatomy: Four muscles on the front of the thigh that extend the knee. Women are often naturally quad-dominant, so form adjustments can help balance the load
            • Best Exercises:
            • Barbell or Goblet Squats
            • Walking or Reverse Lunges
            • Bulgarian Split Squats (closer foot stance)
            • Leg Extensions (isolation)

            2. Hamstrings (Back of Thighs)

            • Anatomy: Three muscles running down the back of the thigh that bend the knee and extend the hip. Strengthening these helps protect the knees and create a balanced leg shape.
            • Best Exercises:
            • Romanian Deadlifts (RDLs)
            • Seated or Lying Leg Curls
            • Single-Leg Romanian Deadlifts

            3. Glutes (Buttocks & Hips)

            • Anatomy: Comprises the gluteus maximus, medius, and minimus. They power hip extension, stabilization, and shaping.
            • Best Exercises:
            • Barbell Hip Thrusts
            • Sumo Squats
            • Curtsy Lunges
            • Glute Bridges

            5. Adductors and Abductors (Inner & Outer Thighs)

            • Anatomy: Stabilizers that control side-to-side leg movement and hip alignment.
            • Best Exercises:
            • Lateral Lunges (Side Lunges)
            • Hip Adductor / Abductor Machines
            • Banded Lateral Monster Walks
