        <section class="run">
          <h1>cardio</h1>
          <p>
            here are different cardio options depednig on your health goals:
            Fat Loss & Metabolism Boost
            • Best Practice: High-Intensity Interval Training (HIIT) combined with strength training.
            • Why: Alternating short bursts of maximum effort (like sprint intervals or HIIT bikes) with recovery burns significant calories quickly and elevates your metabolic rate post-workout.

            • Heart Health & Stress Reduction (Cortisol Management)
            • Best Practice: Zone 2 steady-state cardio (brisk walking, light cycling, or swimming).
            • Why: Keeping your heart rate at 60–70% of its maximum allows you to hold a conversation while building your aerobic base, improving mitochondrial function, and keeping stress hormones like cortisol balanced.

            • Joint Protection & Longevity
            • Best Practice: Low-impact steady-state options like swimming, cycling, or incline walking.
            • Why: These deliver strong cardiovascular and post-menopausal heart benefits without placing heavy shock-loading stress on the ankles, knees, or hips.

            • Total-Body Toning & Muscle Preservation
            • Best Practice: Circuit training or full-body ergometers (rowing, stair climbing).
            • Why: Rowing and circuit routines engage both upper and lower muscle groups simultaneously, merging aerobic conditioning with muscular endurance.
          </p>
        </section>

